{
  "behaviorChanges": [
    "CI runner routing now asserts where a job actually ran. Six locally-routed jobs (validate, ci-python x2, ci-python-full x3) invoke .github/actions/assert-runner-identity immediately after checkout.",
    "On the canonical repository an unset CI_RUNNER_LABEL now FAILS the run. To take billed hosted runs deliberately -- the local runner is away -- set CI_ALLOW_HOSTED_FALLBACK=1 as well; affected jobs then pass with a ::warning on every run, so an open hatch stays visible rather than being found on an invoice.",
    "Forks are unaffected: the action short-circuits for any repository other than the canonical one, because hosted compute is the only thing a fork has. That comparison is case-insensitive -- an exact compare would read the canonical repo as a fork whenever the slug casing differed, and the guard would bypass itself.",
    "The assertion cannot detect an offline, deregistered, or typoed runner label, and does not claim to: GitHub queues those jobs rather than falling back to hosted, so no step runs. That case has its own signal -- nothing merges.",
    "The workflow SHA-pin guard now exempts same-repo ./ action references, keyed on the ./ prefix rather than on the absence of an @pin, and additionally covers ci-python-full.yml, which had been left out of it."
  ],
